.TH VAULT-ADD 1 "October 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-add \- encrypt files, directories or URLs into the vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault add
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-bytes
.IR SIZE ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR DURATION ]
.IR FILE | DIR | URL
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encrypts a file into the vault, named after its base name. A directory is
added recursively, keeping its structure beneath its own name; a directory
named "." or ".." adds its contents directly. Non-regular files, the vault
and the key are skipped. A stored name that already exists is replaced.
.PP
An \fBhttp://\fR or \fBhttps://\fR \fIURL\fR is downloaded with a Chrome user
agent and stored under the last element of its final (post-redirect) path, or
the host name if there is none. Only a 200 response is accepted. Certificates
are always verified; at most 10 redirects are followed, to http or https
only. The download is staged in a private temporary file (it must be
complete before it can be stored), which is removed afterwards whatever
happens; it is plaintext on disk meanwhile.
.PP
A file that changes while it is being added (it grows, shrinks, or is
replaced) is not stored, and the command fails.
.PP
\fIFOLDER\fR places the result inside a folder in the vault. File contents
are cut into 4 MiB chunks, the last bucket-padded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-bytes " SIZE"
Largest download accepted, counted after decompression, such as 500M or 50G.
Default 16G; at most 1T.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Deadline for the whole download, such as 30m. Default 2h. Connecting must
take under 30 seconds and the response headers must arrive within a minute.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
vault add report.pdf work/2026
vault add ./photos
vault add https://example.com/paper.pdf papers
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-migrate (1),
.BR vault\-mirror (1),
.BR vault\-absorb (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
